# AI Agent Behavior Rules — RETIRED (P4)

This rule was an `alwaysApply: true` session-wide card. It is **retired**, not
deleted, so that any surviving reference to it resolves to a pointer instead of
silently loading stale guidance.

**Why:** it duplicated `AGENTS.md` almost line for line, and its one non-
duplicated section was dead. The "Session alerts" table instructed the agent to
read `Saved/Logs/automation_tasks_complete.md`, `automation_exit_alert.md`,
`automation_last_completion.json`, `automation_heartbeat.log`,
`automation_status_latest.txt` and `automation_terminal_capture.log` at the
start of every session. Those files still exist on disk because the WAVE F
agent-company loop that wrote them was deleted, so they are frozen stale
output: an agent was being told to read a heartbeat that can no longer update.

Retiring it also closes the `docs/Setup/DOCTOR_POLICY.md` finding **"Always-
Applied Rule Budget Exceeded"** (HR-B2 had already cut 15 → 3; this takes 3 → 0).

